  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australian National University (ANU) Philippines Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ANU Philippines Project is a partnership between DFAT and the Australian National University (ANU) to support the ANU Philippines Institute. The goals are to foster deeper bilateral ties between Australia and the Philippines through stronger institutional and people-to-people links, and support policymaking and reform in critical areas informed by relevant, high-quality policy research and analysis. The project fosters research, policy analysis, and bilateral collaborations across seven core themes by working to develop stronger research practices, scholarly exchanges and deeper research-to-policy engagement.</narrative>
  </description>
